  "id": "COMPOUND:3933 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Digitoxigenin is implicated in the regulation of CD276 antigen through a multi-step mechanism involving SK-HEP1 cells. The evidence suggests that Digitoxigenin acts as a target for SK-HEP1, which in turn is targeted by two different compounds—Polymatin A and Massarinin B—both of which ultimately lead to the activation of CD276 antigen. This indicates that Digitoxigenin may exert its effects through a shared or related pathway that influences SK-HEP1 and subsequently CD276. The presence of a third compound, [(1R,2R,3S,8R,10R,11S,12R,14R,16S,17R,18R,19R)-3-acetyloxy-16-(furan-3-yl)-18,19-dihydroxy-2,7,7,11,17-pentamethyl-5-oxo-6,13-dioxapentacyclo[9.8.0.02,8.012,14.012,17]nonadecan-10-yl] acetate, which also targets CD276, further supports the notion that the interaction between Digitoxigenin and CD276 is part of a broader network of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways suggests that Digitoxigenin may modulate CD276 expression through SK-HEP1, potentially influencing immune or tumor-related processes. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Digitoxigenin and CD276, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
